\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Dose-response, $n{=}64$ per rung. \textbf  {range (sd)} is the best-to-worst span in units of the metric's own noise floor, given as $n{=}64$\,/\,$n{=}128$ where both were run. The render metric is perfectly monotone on two axes and \emph  {flat} on the third; on that axis its rank correlation is unstable between the two runs ($+0.300$ vs $+0.900$), being the correlation of a sequence that does not move, so read the span instead. A resolution axis was dropped: changing a build's resolution changes its size, not its quality (\S  \ref {sec:setting}).}}{17}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
