\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Retraining on a clean split collapses the margin. \mbox  {V-KID}{} at $n{=}128$, $399$-build reference, paired and Holm-corrected over all $153$ pairs with an exact label-permutation test. Letters mark maximal sets of arms that no test separated at $\alpha =0.05$: a shared letter means the pair was \emph  {not separated}, never that the arms are equivalent, and an arm carries several letters when non-separation fails to be transitive, as it does here. The contaminated arm is not separated from either its own clean retrain or the stronger language-model baseline, and the clean retrain ties with both baselines it had appeared to beat.}}{18}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
