\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Procedural baselines, with real held-out data for reference. \mbox  {\textsc  {Gabled-House}}{} is the bar that matters: what a competent afternoon of hand-written rules produces. \mbox  {\textsc  {Patch-Stitch}}{} is an attack, not a baseline. Every cell is a per-build mean over $n{=}128$ builds per baseline; the real row is all $399$ held-out test builds. \textbf  {Interior is reported twice}, because the two counters answer different questions (Appendix~\ref {app:interior}): \emph  {sealed} is air unreachable from the bounding box, \emph  {open} additionally credits rooms reachable only through a door or window. The distinction is not cosmetic: \mbox  {\textsc  {Gabled-House}}{} has a doorway, so it scores $0.000$ sealed and $0.562$ open.}}{20}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
